# Strings & constants

## UI strings
- **No hardcoded user-facing text anywhere** (shared, androidMain/iosMain/js/wasm, webApp master): screens, VMs, snackbars, notifications, dialogs, `contentDescription`, platform error messages, payment descriptions, enum labels shown in UI.
- Every string lives in `shared/src/commonMain/composeResources/values/strings.xml` (default **en**) and is used only via `stringResource(Res.string.x)` / `getString(...)` (suspend) / `UiText.res(...)` / `StringResource` fields.
- Platform code that reports an error to the UI passes a `StringResource` (e.g. `SpeechEvent.Error`), never raw text.
- **Translate every new/changed string in all supported locales** (`values-hi`, `values-kn`, `values-pa`, `values-mr`, `values-bn` — see `AppLanguage`) in the same change. Keep keys, placeholders (`%1$s`, `%1$d`, `%%`) and escaping identical.
- Allowed literals: log/exception messages never shown to users, analytics keys, animation labels, ids/codes.

## Product names (data i18n)
- Product names are data, not resources: English `name` + per-language `translations` map (lang code → name).
- Show names via `Product.displayName(languageCode)` / `localizedName` helpers, never `product.name` directly in UI.

## Constants
- Never scatter magic strings/numbers for prefs keys, shop ids, language codes, notification channels, delays, etc.
- Put shared app-wide constants in `shared/.../util/AppConstants.kt` (`object AppConstants`).
- Create or extend `AppConstants` when a new shared constant is needed; prefer reusing existing entries over duplicating.
- Feature-private constants may stay as `private const` in that feature/file when they are not reused.
